# provenance: the WorldEntityKernelProjection consumption step
# (WorldEntityKernelProjection.cs:50-97 + EntityEventSync.cs:102-119)
# — the late-joiner one-shot consumption was LOG-ONLY until the phase-5 fix
# (2026-08-12), then moved from the legacy TrapStateSnapshot wire to the kernel
# checkpoint projection. Two entities consumed; the checkpoint arrives; the
# late joiner replays both (the relays from the triggering frame already
# consumed the per-entity guard once — the checkpoint entries are dropped as
# duplicates, which is exactly the idempotency the design relies on); the
# duplicate checkpoint resend must NOT re-consume.
# Mechanism: KernelEnvelope (NetMsg 122) + WorldEntityKernelProjection.
@0 event g1 MineExploded 10 20
@0 event g1 BioTerminalUnlocked 30 40
@33 expect executed MineExploded 1 within 500
@33 expect executed BioTerminalUnlocked 1 within 500
@33 checkpoint g2
@66 expect replayed g2 MineExploded 1 within 500
@66 expect replayed g2 BioTerminalUnlocked 1 within 500
@66 checkpoint g2
@99 expect replayed g2 MineExploded 1 within 500
@99 expect replayed g2 BioTerminalUnlocked 1 within 500
